From misc.legal Thu Mar  7 08:46:40 1991
Path: ux1.cso.uiuc.edu!uwm.edu!cs.utexas.edu!swrinde!mips!dimacs.rutgers.edu!rutgers!mcnc!taco!ccvr1.ncsu.edu!hes
From: hes@ccvr1.ncsu.edu (Henry E. Schaffer)
Newsgroups: misc.legal
Subject: Pledge - history of "under God" phrase
Keywords: recent
Message-ID: <1991Mar7.023430.18615@ncsu.edu>
Date: 7 Mar 91 02:34:30 GMT
Sender: news@ncsu.edu (USENET News System)
Reply-To: hes@ccvr1.ncsu.edu (Henry E. Schaffer)
Organization: NCSU Computing Center
Lines: 9


  According to my encyclopedia, the Pledge was first published in
1892.  In 1923 the phrase "the flag of the United States of
America" was substituted for the previous "my flag" and the Pledge
was adopted by Congress in 1942.

  In 1954, the phrase "under God" was added.

--henry schaffer  n c state univ

From misc.legal Fri Mar  8 08:06:51 1991
