From: riddle@hoss.unl.edu (Michael H. Riddle)
Subject: UN Resolutions Online
Message-ID: <1991Mar08.000429.28923@hoss.unl.edu>
Summary: UN Resolutions and Documents available in electronic form.
Keywords: UN Resolution
Sender: news@hoss.unl.edu (Network News Administer)
Cc: unitex@ieee.org,riddle
Organization: University of Nebraska - Lincoln
Date: Fri, 08 Mar 91 00:04:29 GMT
Lines: 92

A while ago I posted some UN resolutions to misc.legal.  In response to
a number of netmail inquiries, and with Dr. James Waldron's permission,
I am posting the following to the net.  Please address any inquiries to
Dr. Waldron at the addresses listed in the text below.  
 
"I'm only the messenger."


         U N I T E X    C O M M U N I C A T I O N S
         ____________________________________________
 
  UNitex Communications is a small, New Jersey based non-profit
  organization engaged in two fundamental areas of research &
  development, collectively know as the UNitex Project which consist of:
  
     A. Electronic information processing 
        and distribution. UN information 
 
     B. Software design, development 
        and systems integration 
   
  The UNitex Project has completed a 2 year pilot study in the areas of
  specialized information distribution using the latest microcomputer
  technology.  The focus of our research and development is in
  distributed network and wide-area network software development,
  electronic mail systems, database management systems and library 
  retrieval information systems. The application has been in the
  electronic dissemination and distribution of United Nations
  information and the tranfser of appropriate technologies to
  facilitate that goal.
  
  A principal conclusion from the UNitex Project is that a very
  cost-effective alternative to expensive online information systems is
  now available.  In place of hourly rates, setup fees, carrier-connect
  charges and data volume charges, a distributed information system can
  drastically reduce costs and can greatly simplfy the user-interface
  and facilitate the access of information since information is sent or
  delivered to the site without the burden of lengthy online searches.
   
  UNitex supplies current news and information from:
  
  # UN General Assembly Proceedings
  # UN Security Council Resolutions
  # Special UN Committee Papers and Dsicussions
  # UN Press Releases
  # UNCED (UN Committee on Environemnt & Development) 
  # UNICEF News Flashes, Special Announcements, Press Releases
  # International News Briefings from UN Agencies 
  # Related News and Press Briefings (DOD, WHO, etc)
  # Calendar of Meetings and UN Agenda
  
  This information can be readily delivered, electronically, to a
  school or university for a fraction of the cost of commercial on-line
  services. In fact, most of the information that we distribute is not
  readily available from any service.  The average weekly deliverly
  contains approximately 50 to 75 pages (200 to 300K) of useful data,
  news and international journalism. Private individual subscriptions
  are also available. 
  
  UNITEX promotes the Model UN Program and provides data, information
  and courseware for participants.
  
  If your school is a University or College and is connected to the
  InterNet, UseNet or BitNet, we can arrange for imediate delivery.  If
  your high school has PC'S or MacIntosh's and modems, we can arrange
  for delivery to your location.
  
  FOR MORE INFORMATION AND A BROCHURE ON UNITEX,
  PLEASE CALL (201) 677-1563 TODAY!
  
  OR WRITE TO:
      
  UNITEX Communications
  James Waldron, Ph.D 
  Senior Director
  P.O. Box 70
  Glen Ridge, NJ 07028
  
   Voice:   (201) 677-1563
  Support BBS:   (201) 678-1367  9600,2400,1200 Baud
     InterNet:   unitex@IEEE.ORG
   Compuserve:   [75006,156] c/o Robert Flowers, Associate Director
  
  
  
  

