In <1991Sep2.181030.5763@bradley.bradley.edu> pwh@bradley.bradley.edu
(Pete Hartman) writes:

>What is wrong with an oath that doesn't rely on religious grounds?
[...]
>Like "I hereby swear to tell the truth, the whole truth, and nothing
>but the truth."  Period.

The word "swear" is usally replaced with the phrase "swear or affirm"
because "to swear" is "to make a solemn declaration or statement with
an appeal to God" [OEDII].

- Carl
