The law basically says that you don't have to give IGA your SS# and
they don't have to accept your check. In other words, you and IGA are
in a stand off.

> Also, strategies from anyone who has dealt with this
>before would be handy.

Try saying "I'm sorry that information is not available." (This often
works with phone numbers on credit card slips.)

Or, "May I see a written rule requiring disclosure of this personal
information?"

- Carl
