[...]
>Do you know any more about this?  Is it somehow Texas law that atheists
>cannot serve on juries, or have there just been cases of atheists being
>dismissed "without cause"?

I'm sorry I don't have references. I only know what I see on
public-access cable :-)

Texas *requires* potential jurors and actual jurors to swear to God.
This is uncommon, in other contexts a person may either swear *or*
affirm. Apparently, this has gone all the way to the Supreme Court
with the Court deciding that atheists have no right to serve on a
jury.
-- 
