Path: m.cs.uiuc.edu!ux1.cso.uiuc.edu!uwm.edu!zaphod.mps.ohio-state.edu!rphroy!cfctech!kevin
From: kevin@cfctech.cfc.com (Kevin Darcy)
Newsgroups: misc.legal
Subject: Re: Supreme Court Decisions via ftp?
Keywords: supreme, court, ftp
Message-ID: <1991Nov21.035313.23913@cfctech.cfc.com>
Date: 21 Nov 91 03:53:13 GMT
References: <746@shrike.com>
Distribution: usa
Organization: Chrysler Financial Corp., Southfield, MI
Lines: 33

In article <746@shrike.com> p667343@austin.lockheed.com (p667343) writes:
>I have heard that Supreme Court decisions can be obtained via ftp.  If this
>is true, what are the archive sites?
>
>Thanks
>
>Tom Benjamin

(From memory...)

uunet.uu.net, in /pub/opinions
ftp.cwru.edu, in /hermes/ascii

Note that these sites take the raw typeset files from the SC Publications 
Office and convert them to ascii. They do NOT use the same conversion program/
script, so the output formats differ considerably. I prefer the cwru 
formatting myself, although both formats have minor imperfections, and I'll
probably write my own (perfect :-) conversion script when I get some time 
Real Soon Now. 

Organizationally, uunet keeps each decision in its own directory, whereas cwru 
keeps them all in one directory. Which is more convenient would depend on how 
many decisions you want to download, etc.

Does anyone know if Project Hermes is still in operation? Last time I looked
(a week or two ago), I couldn't find any decisions for the current term.
								
