I have an unusual request.

Some friends of mine, who work on a student newspaper, have asked me
to give a presentation on the first amendment rights of newspapers,
with special emphasis on libel law.

I've agreed, but unfortunately, I don't currently have access to a
decent law library, and I need to dig up some of the important Supreme
Court cases on the subject.

So I'm sending out a call to anyone who might have access to Supreme Court
opinions on-line to help me out by sending me copies of the following
by computer mail.

Thanks in advance.

larry kolodney


Here's what I need:

New York Times v. Sullivan, 376 U.S. 254
Associated Press v. Walker, 388 U.S. 130
Curtis PUblishing CO. v. BUtts, 388 U.S. 130
Gertz v. Robert Welch, Inc., 418 U.S. 323
Time, Inc. v. Firestone, 424 U.S. 448
