=================
README
=================
Directory of general documents related to government. It includes the
U.S. Constitution and mailing addresses for U.S. Senators and
Representatives.

The archive is accessible via anonymous ftp and email. Ftp to
ftp.eff.org (192.88.144.4). It is in directory "pub/academic/civics".
For email access, send email to archive-server@eff.org. Include the
line:
      civics <filenames>
where <filenames> is a list of the files that you want. File README is
a detailed description of the items in the directory.

=================
administration.address
=================
Addresses for writing to the President, the Vice-President, and
cabinet members.

=================
congress.address
=================
A list of U.S. Senators and Representatives. The list includes
name, party, hometown, DC telephone, and committee assignments.

=================
constitution.us
=================
The Constitution of the United States

=================
dec_of_ind
=================
The Declaration of Independence

=================
fcc
=================
Address, names, and fax number for the Federal Communications Commission

=================
foia
=================
The file is for individuals or organizations who wish to make an
Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) application to a federal agency.

=================
gov.contact
=================
Tells how to call a representive or senator, how to call the White House
(comment line, fax, general), how to write Congress or the White House.
Also, gives names of key leaders of congress.

- Carl

=================
house-of-reps.tel-and-fax
=================
House of Representatives faxes and phones

=================
judiciary.fax
=================
The fax numbers of the members of the Senate judiciary committee.

=================
media.fax
=================
Fax numbers for major media.

=================
senate.label-ready
=================
Mailing labels for U.S. Senators

=================
=================
Last update
Sat Mar 21 14:30:11 EST 1992
