mmwang@adobe.com (Michael Wang) writes:

>Is there a publication or book/almanac that summarizes all the
>Supreme Court decisions for a given year? I'm looking for something
>that gives at least some analysis for each of the decisions since
>just reading Court opinions can be a bit mystifying to somebody
>who knows little about Constitutional law. 
[...]

This is quite what you were asking for, but it is on-line
and free.

- Carl

======== ftp.eff.org:pub/law/court-decisions ============
If you are on the Internet, you can do text searches on Supreme Court
decisions with WAIS. For info on WAIS, look at newsgroup alt.wais. You
can access a WAIS client by:
  telnet quake.think.com
OR
  telnet hub.nnsc.nsf.net

Login as "wais".

Decisions are also available via ftp if you know the case number.
Information is enclosed.

- Carl
---------
