Organization: Amdahl Corporation, Sunnyvale CA
Lines: 39

In article <9208041637.AA22883@aslss01> murthy@ssd.dl.nec.com (Vasudev Murthy) writes:
>I believe there is some way in which Lexis and WESTLAW can be accessed
>from Internet (anonymous logins or something). Can someone tell me how I
>can go about this? Which sites allow such access?

LEXIS:

Using telnet, you can connect to Lexis at lexis.mdc.org or
lexis.meaddata.com (192.73.216.20).  When prompted for a terminal type,
enter ".vt100a" (without quotes).  I receive garbage, though, and no
amount of tweaking with "stty" seems to help.

An alternative that does work for me is to telnet to the Merit Computer
Network at hermes.merit.edu (35.1.48.149).  When prompted "Which Host?",
reply "lexis", then respond as indicated above.

Once in, you will be restricted to the commands; that is, the function
keys will not function.  Frustrating to have to do four keystrokes to get
to the next page, but it works.

WESTLAW:

I have no direct IP address (anyone?).

You can connect to WestLaw via the hermes.merit.edu connection mentioned
above for Lexis, but I'm unaware of how to anwer the prompts.  You will
get no prompt until you hit return once, then you get "please enter system
select character".

You will still need a valid Lexis and/or Westlaw ID, once connected, of
course.

I'd love it if anyone can tell me how to connect directly to Mead, or how
to connect to WestLaw by any method.
