Date: Wed, 12 Aug 1992 17:15:37 GMT

fsars@acad3.alaska.edu (Allen R Sparks) writes:

[...]
>I'd like to know what changes Pennsylvania's ERA had in that state,
>how involved the state court system was, and what kind of political
>pressures judges have to endure.  === Al Sparks
[...]

Illinois has equal rights in the state constitution since the '70's.
Contrary to some predictions, we have not had to share bathrooms.

The main effect has been that laws no longer make assumptions about
the sexes. For example, the alimony law no longer presumes that the
husband earns more than the wife.

- Carl


