the sense of what should be legally allowable, specifically I was
under the impression that the topic of this thread whether "hate
speech" should be legally allowed.

I was further confused by your phrasing. The phrasing I would have
expected for the meaning you (of course) meant was: "It is never right
to commit a moral wrong". I believe your phrasing is the first time
I've heard "right"-as-morally-correct used a noun and preceded by "a",
except in the idiom "two wrongs don't make a right."

I was also confused by the context of your reply. Recall that your
reply was in response to a paragraph of mine that started:

cmk> As for legality:
cmk> Many religious groups exclude nonmembers, it is legal.

I apologize for assuming that your reply, addressed my paragraph.

- Carl
