pas@cc.gatech.edu (Paulo Santos) writes:

>Is it legal to record conversations (meetings, etc.) without everyone
>involved explicitly knowing that they are being recorded?
[...]

Here is a procedure that I think is prudent (it was used in parts of
IBM 10 or so years ago):

Before turning on the tape recorder, ask "Is it ok if I tape record
our meeting?"

Is there are no objections, turn it on and say "For the record, is it
ok if I tape record our meeting".

- Carl

