kadie@uiuc.edu (Carl Kadie writes:

>Amendment 2 doesn't even ban all laws that prohibit private
>discrimination on the basis of sexual orientation, it only bans
>(enforcement of) laws that prohibit discrimination on the basis of
>*gay* sexual orientation.

a_rubin@dsg4.dse.beckman.com (Arthur Rubin) writes:

[...]
>Now THAT is a more serious problem.  But there aren't any laws that
>discriminate on the basis of heterosexual orientation, are there? :-)
[...]

The cites of Boulder, Denver, and Aspen prohibit some forms of
discrimination (e.g. housing, employment) on the basis of sexual
orientation (race, religion, sex, etc). If the amendent goes into
force, the cities will not be allowed to take action against
discrimination against gays, but they will still be able to take
action against discrimination against straights.

- Carl

