jdonahue@essential.org (JIM@essential.org) writes:

>Regulation has always been content-neutral.  See your history.

The FCC bans "indecent" content.

It also has rules on so-called personal attacks and editorials by
broadcasters. It used to have the so-called fairness doctrine.

None of these regulations would be allowed for a public park or a
student newspaper at a state university because they are not content
neutral.

- Carl
