Newsgroups: misc.legal
Path: cs.uiuc.edu!kadie
From: kadie@cs.uiuc.edu (Carl M Kadie)
Subject: Re: Publication of Letters?
Message-ID: <CD9qwG.Bqx@cs.uiuc.edu>
Organization: University of Illinois, Dept. of Comp. Sci., Urbana, IL
References: <feustelCD42tD.59r@netcom.com> <bazz023o4fqa01@JUTS.ccc.amdahl.com> <1993Sep12.112522.17878@newstand.syr.edu>
Date: Mon, 13 Sep 1993 01:31:27 GMT
Lines: 17

Here is my, nonlaywer, opinion:

Fair use should include:
  Printing at least one paper copy.
  Publishing short excerpts or the whole letter if it is short.

It should also be ok to:
   Show people your on-screen or paper copy.
   Tell people the gist of the letter.

Put another way, the only thing that should be a violation of copyright
would be publishing large parts of a large letter.

- Carl
-- 
Carl Kadie -- I do not represent any organization; this is just me.
 = kadie@cs.uiuc.edu =

