j724664s@edinboro.edu writes:

[...]
>The bulk of the argument was: If it is only chalk and temporary, is it
>still vandalism?  There is no intent of malice and this same technique
>is used often by the student body of Slippery Rock university (of course
>I think they have permission).  Nothing like this is covered, I think, in
>university policy.
[...]

I personally don't think that it is vandalism; I'd say it is a common
and accepted means of expression at universities all over the nation.

If Edinboro wanted to it could probably ban this means of expression,
but it couldn't do so just because it doesn't like gay messages.  If,
for example, it has in the past allowed the young Republicans to chalk
the sidewalks, then it can't punish a gay group for doing the same.

- Carl

