In <a_rubin.761011853@dn66>, a_rubin@dsg4.dse.beckman.com sez:
>In <1994Feb11.233907.28587@gallant.apple.com> David Casseres <casseres@apple.com> writes:
>
>>As a matter of fact the ACLU has stood up for the rights of a lot of
>>individuals and organizations on the Right.
>
>True, but only from a left-wing perspective.  For instance, they opposed
>the rights of a 12-year-old (Soviet) to apply for asylum.

Too bad you don't tell the full story.  The child's parents wanted to
return to the Soviet Union, and wanted their child to go with them
(duh).  The ACLU took the uncontroversial position that parents have a
strong -- dare I say constitutional? -- liberty interest in raising
their children as they see fit.

The flip side, of course, is that Ed Meese's DoJ took the position
that a 12-year-old child ought to be able to oppose his parents (and
obtain separate counsel) in legal proceedings -- a position that is
regularly branded "left-wing" when identified with Hillary Clinton.

You know better than to engage in this sort of rank deceit, Arthur.

